eat wind.\n\nReason: W7 is completely isolated with no connecting tiles in my hand and limited unshown copies (only 2). Discarding it maintains maximum flexibility with my T1 pung, and the B5-B6 pairs which have the best potential to form chows with abundant B4 tiles (4 unshown). This keeps my hand compact and focused on achievable patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play W7"}
