ecome pair)\n\nThis maximizes my flexibility with two potential complete chows and a pung already formed.\n\nReason: T2 is an isolated tile that doesn't contribute to any strong sequence formation. By discarding it, I maintain T1\u00d73 (pung), can form T4-T5-T6 and B4-B5-B6 sequences, creating a clearer path to a complete hand. The remaining tiles have better synergy for forming standard four-melds-plus-pair pattern.\n\nAnswer: Play T2"}
